              "ImageDescription": {
                "value": "<span>An encrusted copper-alloy nummus of Crispus (</span>AD<span> 317- 326), dating to </span>AD<span> 318-319 (Reece Period 16),CRISPVS NOB CAES; laureate and cuirassed bust left with spear pointing forward, shield on left arm. VIRTVS AVGG; open camp gate (no door) with four turrets. Mint of Rome. RIC VII, p. 316, no. 191. The recorded specimen in Vienna is from Officina S; this coin appears to be from Officina P. The British Museum has no example of this type for Crispus at all.</span>",
